From: André Valentin <avalentin@marcant.net>
Subject: env: sf: skip redundant read when no redundant offset is configured

When CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND is unset, ENV_OFFSET_REDUND is
OFFSET_INVALID (0xffffffff) and env_sf_load() still performs the
second SPI read at that offset. On some flashes this read has
unwanted side effects (and it is pointless anyway). Skip it.

--- a/env/sf.c
+++ b/env/sf.c
@@ -184,8 +184,11 @@
 
 	read1_fail = spi_flash_read(env_flash, CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET,
 				    CONFIG_ENV_SIZE, tmp_env1);
-	read2_fail = spi_flash_read(env_flash, CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND,
-				    CONFIG_ENV_SIZE, tmp_env2);
+	if (ENV_OFFSET_REDUND == OFFSET_INVALID)
+		read2_fail = 1;
+	else
+		read2_fail = spi_flash_read(env_flash, CONFIG_ENV_OFFSET_REDUND,
+					    CONFIG_ENV_SIZE, tmp_env2);
 
 	ret = env_import_redund((char *)tmp_env1, read1_fail, (char *)tmp_env2,
 				read2_fail, H_EXTERNAL);
